<title>UK: Simon denies it had takeover approach.</title>
<headline>Simon denies it had takeover approach.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Simon Engineering Plc said on Thursday that contrary to recent press speculation it had not received a takeover approach.  </p>
<p>Newspaper reports said there was talk that Rutland Trust Plc was likely to bid for Simon Engineering.</p>
<p>Simon said in a statement that it has had informal discussions with Rutland &quot;regarding the opportunities for the port related activities of the two groups&quot;.</p>
<p>The company also revealed that it is exploring a number of options in both the storage and process engineering industries designed to enhance shareholder value.</p>
<p>Simon shares were up 1/2p at 44p by 1033 GMT, after gaining 4p on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
